  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Aesculioside B may interact with the CD276 antigen, through a series of molecular targets. Aesculioside B is directly linked to WI-38 cells, which are then targeted by Taiwanin E and Cyclo(L-Phe-L-Leu), both of which ultimately target the CD276 antigen. This indicates that Aesculioside B may act through a chain of molecular interactions, with the CD276 antigen being a downstream target in this pathway. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway implies that Aesculioside B may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially involving multiple cellular processes. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Aesculioside B could be a candidate for targeting CD276 antigen in therapeutic contexts, provided further experimental validation is conducted.",
